{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"ddd81281-6c86-4f78-b856-917fbefe42e0","step_index":6,"state":"DONE","step_type":"subagent","tool_name":"invoke_subagent","duration_seconds":0.267187103,"subagent_info":{"subagents":[{"type_name":"reviewer","role":"Opamp Reviewer","initial_prompt":"Review the tutor's opamp sizing session. Read AGENTS.md first. Then use get_status to see the best designs, explain what the RL found relative to the tutor's nominal design, check the margins and the area-current trade-off, and write the final summary. Write a log_entry and return ≤ 80 words.\n\nTutor's summary:\n## Tutor summary (101 simulations total)\n\n**Circuit:** Stage 1 = diff pair mn1/mp1 (gm1, first gain); Stage 2 = mp3/mn5 CS (gm6, second gain); Miller Cc+Rc compensates. Cc fights SR vs PM; Rc places LHP zero for PM boost.\n\n**Nominal** (from equations): mn4=18, mn5=18, mp3=20 (balanced: mp3/mp1=2=2×mn5/mn4), mn1=24, cap=2pF, res=1500Ω, all L=90nm. I_tail=60µA, I2=60µA, total≈150µA. Simulated: gain=678✓, SR=22.4✗, UGBW=20.6MHz✗, PM=36°✗.\n\n**Search space:** mn1[14–24], mn4[13–23], mn5[13–23], mp3[15–24], cap[1p–3p], res[700–1700]. All L, W, mn3, mp1 fixed. 11 grid points each. L fixed because different L breaks mirror balance in 45nm.\n\n**Key sensitivities (warm-up):**\n- res: PM ±8%/step — most efficient PM lever\n- mn4: UGBW/SR ±10%/step\n- cap: SR/UGBW ±7%, PM ±4%, area ±8%/step\n- mn5/mp3: PM ±5–6%/step\n- mn1: very weak (\u003c1%/step) — almost frozen\n\n**RL (80 sims):** reward -0.886→-0.772. Best: mn4=23(max), mn1=23, mn5=21, mp3=22, cap=1.5pF. SR=31.2V/µs✓, gain=652✓, noise=22mV✓, current=178µA✓, area=637µm²✓ — UGBW=29.6MHz✗, PM=35.4°✗.\n\n**Refine (4 designs):** Coupled push cap→1pF + mn5=23, mp3=24, mn4=23, res=1700 → reward -0.681 (best). UGBW +29.5%, SR +25.3% vs RL best. Still no all-specs pass: UGBW~38MHz (need 100) and PM~34.7° (need 60°) remain hard gaps.\n\n**Root cause:** The search space hit its ceiling on all fast-spec levers (mn4=max, cap=min, res=max). The 100MHz UGBW target requires either broader mn1 range (beyond 24), or wider W, or the reviewer should note the fundamental topology constraint.","conversation_id":"e82d8654-aa1f-4bc6-b36c-b8de30d342d0","log_uri":"file:///home/brentvm/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/e82d8654-aa1f-4bc6-b36c-b8de30d342d0/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl","workspace_uris":["file:///home/brentvm/projects/CAICD-shared/CAD"]}]}}}
